course: dictionary
lesson: 9313
title: Compound words: speedboat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A speedboat is a small, fast boat with a powerful engine. Its name is built from two smaller words, speed and boat, joined together. A word made like this is called a compound word, and you can often work out its meaning by splitting it into parts.
explain: The context helps too. «Their longships were light and fast and could sail up shallow rivers, so Vikings could appear far from home without warning, like a speedboat that also fits in a stream.» The words light, fast and fits in a stream are clues that a speedboat is small and quick.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence: «like a small, fast boat that also fits in a stream». It still makes sense, so the meaning works.
fact: A speedboat is a small, fast boat with a powerful engine.
fact: A compound word joins two words to make a new meaning: speed + boat = speedboat.
fact: The plural of speedboat is speedboats.
fact: Speedboat rides happen on lakes and the sea, and you should always wear a life jacket.
fact: Check a compound word by splitting it into its two parts and asking what they mean together.
exercise: What is a speedboat? | A large boat that carries many people slowly | *A small, fast boat with a powerful engine | A fish that swims very quickly | A boat with sails made of paper
exercise: Which two words join to make speedboat? | sped and oar | speed and sea | speedy and bot | *speed and boat
exercise: What should you always wear on a speedboat ride? | A hat with a big brim | Roller skates | *A life jacket | A winter coat
test: «...like a speedboat that also fits in a stream.» What does this comparison tell you about a speedboat? | *It is small and fast | It can fly over the hills | It is huge and slow | It has no engine
test: What is the plural of speedboat? | speedsboat | *speedboats | speedboatts | speedboates
exam: Which sentence uses speedboat correctly? | The speedboat is a bread that rises in the oven. | We ate a speedboat for lunch. | Speedboat is the name of my cat who sleeps all day. | *The speedboat zoomed across the lake, spraying water high.
